# Benefits of Cloud Computing

## Purpose of this Section
Understand **why organizations move to the cloud** and what business and technical benefits cloud computing provides.

## High Availability

- Ability of a system to remain **operational during failures**
- Achieved using redundancy (multiple instances, zones, regions)

**Why it matters:**
- Reduces downtime
- Improves user trust and business continuity

## Scalability

- Ability to **increase or decrease resources** based on demand

Two types:
- **Vertical scaling** – add more power to one resource
- **Horizontal scaling** – add more resources

**Why it matters:**
- Supports business growth without redesigning applications

## Elasticity

- Ability to **automatically scale resources** up or down
- Often implemented using autoscaling

**Why it matters:**
- Saves cost
- Handles sudden traffic spikes efficiently

## Reliability

- Ability of a system to **recover from failures**
- Achieved using backups, replication, and self-healing services

**Why it matters:**
- Ensures systems can continue working after unexpected issues

## Predictability

- Ability to **predict performance and costs**
- Azure provides tools to estimate usage and billing

**Why it matters:**
- Helps in planning budgets and capacity
- Avoids unexpected bill

## Security

- Cloud providers invest heavily in platform security
- Security responsibilities are shared (Shared Responsibility Model)

**Why it matters:**
- Protects data, applications, and infrastructure
- Meets enterprise and compliance standards

## Governance

- Ability to **define and enforce rules and policies**
- Ensures standards are followed across resources

**Why it matters:**
- Maintains compliance
- Prevents misconfigurations

## Manageability

- Centralized management of cloud resources
- Includes monitoring, automation, and templates

**Why it matters:**
- Simplifies operations
- Reduces manual effort and errors

## Exam Tip
> Scalability = manual capacity change  
> Elasticity = automatic capacity change


## 📌 Quick Revision (One-Liners)
- High availability → stay online
- Scalability → handle growth
- Elasticity → auto-scale
- Reliability → recover from failure
- Predictability → forecast cost & performance
- Security → protect resources
- Governance → enforce rules
- Manageability → easy operations
